==Battleground==
*1 [[Teacher Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wall Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 4.33 seconds<sup>130f</sup>.
*1 [[CyberFace]] spawns after 180 seconds<sup>5,400f</sup>.
*1 [[CyberFace]] spawns after 181 seconds<sup>5,430f</sup>.
*1 [[CyberFace]] spawns after 182.67 seconds<sup>5,480f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Because the CyberFaces are buffed beyond belief, players should focus on racking up as much DPS as possible in order to defeat Teacher Bun Bun and melt through the Wall Doges before destroying the base, all within three minutes. Killing the CyberFaces is possible, but not recommended, as the space reserved for them could instead be used to field other DPS units.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] - With very high speed and Massive Damage to Floating, Fishman can outrange Teacher Bun Bun and consistently deal heavy damage to him, likely tearing him down in less than a minute, then continue to contribute DPS on the Wall Doges.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - A powerful rusher whose extreme DPS goes virtually unopposed with only Wall Doges in his way, he can kill the Wall Doges in two attack cycles on any difficulty, allowing other units to quickly enter and secure ground.
*[[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]] - Useful on 4-crown replays, Teacher BearCat's Insane Damage to Traitless tears down the Wall Doges like dominoes and is disposable enough that several can be deployed quickly to demolish any that stands in their way. Its range shouldn't be of any issue, as Wall Doges have minuscule DPS.
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]]/[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] - Cheap high-damage rushers who can easily accumulate DPS over time on the Wall Doges with their single attacks, with Can Can being able actually outrange Bun Bun if covered by meatshields and CC units.
*[[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] - Being able to Slow Floating enemies for 4 seconds at a 20% chance, Sanzo is extremely helpful for impeding Teacher Bun Bun in combination with meatshields, as its 250 range keeps it  and other units safe.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] - A spammable midranger who's Strong Against Floating. From level 40+, she can tank 2 hits against Bun Bun (3 with Survive) before dying, which makes spamming only her early on to quickly accumulate damage on Teacher Bun Bun a very viable strategy, since the stage barely gives you money before the Wall Doges appear.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] - A cheap way to absorb many hits from Teacher Bun Bun. He allows you to stack up Sanzo Cats freely to slow during his downtime, which enables your attackers to kill Teacher Bun Bun unimpeded.

